      "text": "\\(19\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "infinitely many"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "18"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2014-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The logarithms are defined only when \\(x - 40 \\gt 0\\) and \\(60 - x \\gt 0,\\) so \\(40 \\lt x \\lt 60.\\)\n\nWithin this range the inequality becomes \\((x-40)(60-x) \\lt 100,\\) which expands to \\(x^2 - 100x + 2500 \\gt 0,\\) i.e. \\((x-50)^2 \\gt 0.\\) This holds for every \\(x \\ne 50.\\)\n\nThe integers strictly between \\(40\\) and \\(60\\) except \\(50\\) are \\(41, \\ldots, 49\\) and \\(51, \\ldots, 59,\\) which is \\(18\\) values.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Both logarithms require \\(40 \\lt x \\lt 60\\)",
        "Combining gives \\((x-40)(60-x) \\lt 100,\\) which is \\((x-50)^2 \\gt 0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
